#!/usr/bin/perl -wT

##############################################################################
# PURPOSE: calipsoserver - Serve CALIPSO data, subsetted by date/time range,
#          variable, and longitude-latitude box, in ASCII, XDR, MCMC,
#          NetCDF-COARDS, NetCDF-IOAPI and original (compressed tar file of
#          original hdf files) formats for use by other programs (e.g., curl).
#
# NOTES:   Server is WCS-compliant:
#          https://www.opengeospatial.org/standards/wcs
#          https://datafed.net/xs/OpenGIS/wcs/1.0.0/
#          and modeled after a similar webserver application:
#          https://webapps.datafed.net/ogc_EPA.wsfl
#
#          Launches the C programs CALIPSOSubset and XDRConvert
#          which stream the data back on STDOUT.
#
#          Example usage:
#
#          curl -k --silent --retry 0 'https://ofmpub.epa.gov/rsig/rsigserver?\
#          SERVICE=wcs&\
#          VERSION=1.0.0&\
#          REQUEST=GetCoverage&\
#          COVERAGE=calipso.l1.Total_Attenuated_Backscatter_532&\
#          TIME=2022-07-01T23:00:00Z/2022-07-02T00:00:00Z&\
#          BBOX=-120,30,-110,32,0,10000&\
#          FORMAT=ascii'
#
#          NASA Langley contacts for server cain:
#            Main contact: walter.e.baskin@nasa.gov
#            cain SA: karl.birkland@nasa.gov
#            georgina.hayes-crepps@nasa.gov
#            mathew.s.tisdale@nasa.gov
#
#          NASA login account:
#            https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov login rsig password Rsig4444
#          CALIPSO file list:
#            https://asdc.larc.nasa.gov/data/CALIPSO
#
# HISTORY: 2010-02-08 plessel.todd@epa.gov 1-919-541-5500
#
# STATUS:  reviewed tested
##############################################################################

